I do not play nethack on servers.   I prefer not to use the
bandwidth.

I play nethack -- as opposed to other computer games -- because it is
uniquely detailed.  Few other games have such a wide variety of
challenges, or such varied solutions.  For example, when confronted
with overwhelming odds, few games allow you to simply go through the
floor to escape, followed by a trip back up with the equipment later.
Then throw precious equipment into water, and recover it by finding
some method of breathing underwater, then re-build your blanked
scrolls by *writing your own scrolls* with a magic marker.

I play nethack because it's a hard game.  Without restoring from a
saved game, I have won the game all the way through perhaps 11 times
in three years.  It is frustrating, irritating, but generally fair.
My deaths are generally my own fault, not the game's.  This keeps it
interesting when other games -- which I can beat in my sleep -- have
lost my interest, for all their graphics are better.

I hang out here 1) to receive help with my game 2) to help newbies 3)
To enjoy the cameraderie of people who have a shared love of this
crazy game. The number of hardcore nethackers in the world is quite
small.  I'm glad to know them, even the ones who have killfiled me.

